.TH IMG355CTL 1 "October 2026" "img355ctl 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
img355ctl \- configure the Inca IMG\-355GX gaming mouse
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B img355ctl
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B img355ctl
configures the Inca IMG\-355GX gaming mouse (USB ID 30fa:1040) without the
vendor's Windows software: DPI levels, LED colours and effects, button bindings,
media keys and the "fire" repeat interval.
.PP
The mouse cannot report its settings back, so
.B img355ctl
keeps them in a profile file and writes the whole configuration every time a
setting changes, the same way the vendor software does when you press Apply.
Settings are stored in the mouse and survive unplugging.
All button functions, including media keys, are carried out by the mouse
itself; no background program is needed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-profile " FILE"
Use
.I FILE
instead of the default profile (see
.BR FILES ).
.TP
.BI \-\-device " PATH"
Use the given hidraw node instead of detecting the mouse.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the reports that would be sent, one per line in hex
.RB ( GET
for a status read), and do not touch the mouse or save the profile.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
Every command also accepts
.BR \-\-help .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH COMMANDS
Commands that change a setting save the profile and send it to the mouse.
.TP
.B status
Show the detected mouse and the current profile.
.TP
.B apply
Send the profile to the mouse without changing it.
.TP
.B reset
Restore the factory defaults (the same as "Reset" in the vendor software).
.TP
.B actions
List the button functions, media keys and LED effects.
.TP
.BI "dpi " "LEVEL " \fR[\fIVALUE\fR] " \fR[\fB\-\-on\fR|\fB\-\-off\fR] [\fB\-\-active\fR]"
Set the DPI of
.I LEVEL
(1\-6).
.I VALUE
is 200\-2400 in steps of 200 (except 2200) or 3200\-7200 in steps of 800.
.B \-\-off
removes the level from the rotation of the DPI button,
.B \-\-on
puts it back, and
.B \-\-active
makes the mouse start in this level.
At least one level must stay enabled.
.TP
.BI "color " "LEVEL COLOR"
Set the LED colour of
.I LEVEL
(1\-6, or
.B all
for every level), shown by the
.B dpi\-breathing
and
.B static
effects.
.I COLOR
is
.I RRGGBB
hex (with or without
.BR # ,
3\-digit shorthand allowed) or one of
.BR red ", " green ", " blue ", " yellow ", " cyan ", " magenta ", " pink ,
.BR white ", " orange ", " purple ", " black .
The mouse has 4 bits per channel, so close colours may look the same.
.TP
.BI "button " "N ACTION"
Bind button
.I N
(2\-6, numbered as in the vendor software: 2 right, 3 middle, 4 forward,
5 back, 6 the button on top) to
.IR ACTION .
Button 1 always stays the left click.
See
.BR ACTIONS .
.TP
.BI "led " EFFECT " \fR[\fB\-\-speed\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-colors\fR \fILIST\fR]"
Set the LED effect; see
.BR ACTIONS .
.B \-\-speed
is 1\-6.
.B \-\-colors
selects which of the 7 built\-in cycle colours are used, for example
.BR \(dq1 3 5\(dq .
.TP
.BI "fire " MS
Set the repeat interval of the
.B fire
function in milliseconds (8\-2040, rounded down to a multiple of 8).
.SH ACTIONS
Button functions:
.RS
.B middle right back forward dpi\-loop show\-desktop double\-click fire dpi+ dpi\- led\-loop profile\-1 profile\-2 profile\-3 profile\-4
.RE
.PP
Media keys:
.RS
.B browser player mail volume\-up volume\-down previous next mute play\-pause calculator
.RE
.PP
LED effects:
.RS
.B dpi\-breathing cycle\-breathing static flowing\-water mono\-water comet neon ambilight flicker star\-trek ripple enraptured button\-response off
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/img355ctl/profile.ini
The profile (default
.IR ~/.config/img355ctl/profile.ini ).
It is a plain INI file and can be edited by hand; run
.B img355ctl apply
afterwards.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/70\-img355\-mouse.rules
udev rule giving the logged\-in user access to the mouse's hidraw node
(installed by the .deb package; shipped as
.IR contrib/70\-img355\-mouse.rules ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on error (for example the mouse is missing, a value is out of
range or the profile is invalid), 2 on invalid command line usage.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
img355ctl dpi 1 800             # first level: 800 DPI
img355ctl dpi 6 \-\-off           # skip level 6
img355ctl color all red         # every level red
img355ctl led static            # steady colour
img355ctl led comet \-\-speed 2   # slower comet effect
img355ctl led off               # LEDs off
img355ctl button 5 volume\-up    # side button raises the volume
img355ctl \-n reset              # show the factory settings as reports
.fi
.SH NOTES
Without the udev rule only root can open the mouse.
The .deb package installs it; otherwise
.PP
.nf
sudo install \-m 644 contrib/70\-img355\-mouse.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
sudo udevadm control \-\-reload\-rules
.fi
.PP
and plug the mouse in again.
.SH BUGS
Settings cannot be read from the mouse.
If they are changed by other software,
.B img355ctl apply
restores the profile.
.PP
Macros, shortcuts, the other three profiles and the polling rate are not
supported yet.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR img355ctl\-gui ,
the graphical version, which edits the same profile;
.BR hidraw (4),
.BR udev (7)
